{"pageProps":{"page":{"ID":2052,"post_author":"14","post_date":"February 17, 2026","post_date_gmt":"2026-02-17 16:10:18","post_title":"About","post_status":"publish","comment_status":"closed","ping_status":"closed","post_name":"about","post_modified":"2026-09-09 17:00:16","post_modified_gmt":"2026-09-09 17:00:16","guid":"https://pylon-two.vercel.app/?page_id=2052","post_type":"page","filter":"raw","url":"https://pylon-two.vercel.app/about/","header_options":{"header_theme":"white"},"body_color":"white","sections":[{"acf_fc_layout":"section","components":[{"acf_fc_layout":"mastheads","Mastheads":[{"acf_fc_layout":"about_masthead_new","heading":"Rebuilding America’s mortgage infrastructure","heading_highlight":"mortgage infrastructure","story":{"paragraph":"<p>America’s mortgage market is one of the most important financial systems in the world.</p>\n<p>It finances more than $13 trillion of homes, underwrites the middle class, and is the mechanism through which millions of families build wealth.</p>\n<p>And yet the system that produces mortgages still runs like a factory from another era.</p>\n<p>While every other financial instrument has been simplified into an API call, mortgages are still assembled by hand.</p>\n<p>The result is higher costs, slow decisions, and a fragmented system that forces ordinary Americans to absorb the costs.</p>\n<p>Mortgages are the last major financial product that are not programmable.</p>\n<p>We started from zero and created the first vertically integrated mortgage platform that turns origination into a single API.</p>\n<p>Pylon is building <strong>America’s mortgage rails</strong>.</p>\n"}}]}],"padding_top":"large","padding_bottom":"large","inner_spacing":"medium","background":{"background_color":"white"},"change_to":"black"},{"acf_fc_layout":"section","components":[{"acf_fc_layout":"content","content":[{"acf_fc_layout":"investors","heading":"$45M raised from top VCs","institutional_investors":{"heading":"Institutional investors","inve